one cell, then move +1 fret\nFor the descending pass, read the cards in reverse order and move -1 fret\nStandard tuning. Two-octave 6th-string-root natural minor. One completed cell = 30 notes.\nPage 3 of 7\n01  A MINOR\nROOT E5  |  FRAME 4-8\nNotes: A B C D E F G | A B C D E F G A\n30-NOTE TWO-OCTAVE CELL\nDeg|1--2--b3-4--5--b6-b7-1--2--b3-4--5--b6-b7-1--1--b7-b6-5--4--b3-2--1--b7-b6-5--4--b3-2--1--|\nFng|1--3--4--1--3--4--1--3--1--2--4--1--2--4--1--1--4--2--1--4--2--1--3--1--4--3--1--4--3--1--|\ne  |------------------------------------------5--5--------------------------------------------|\nB  |---------------------------------5--6--8--------8--6--5-----------------------------------|\nG  |------------------------4--5--7--------------------------7--5--4--------------------------|\nD  |------------------5--7--------------------------------------------7--5--------------------|\nA  |---------5--7--8--------------------------------------------------------8--7--5-----------|\nE  |5--7--8--------------------------------------------------------------------------8--7--5--|\nReturn to the low root; release pressure; move the entire frame one fret.\nD-start and U-start\n02  BB MINOR\nROOT E6  |  FRAME 5-9\nNotes: Bb C Db Eb F Gb Ab | Bb C Db Eb F Gb Ab Bb\n30-NOTE TWO-OCTAVE CELL\nDeg|1--2--b3-4--5--b6-b7-1--2--b3-4--5--b6-b7-1--1--b7-b6-5--4--b3-2--1--b7-b6-5--4--b3-2--1--|\nFng|1--3--4--1--3--4--1--3--1--2--4--1--2--4--1--1--4--2--1--4--2--1--3--1--4--3--1--4--3--1--|\ne  |------------------------------------------6--6--------------------------------------------|\nB  |---------------------------------6--7--9--------9--7--6-----------------------------------|\nG  |------------------------5--6--8--------------------------8--6--5--------------------------|\nD  |------------------6--8--------------------------------------------8--6--------------------|\nA  |---------6--8--9--------------------------------------------------------9--8--6-----------|\nE  |6--8--9--------------------------------------------------------------------------9--8--6--|\nReturn to the low root; release pressure; move the entire frame one fret.\nD-start and U-start\n03  B MINOR\nROOT E7  |  FRAME 6-10\nNotes: B C# D E F# G A | B C# D E F# G A B\n30-NOTE TWO-OCTAVE CELL\nDeg|1--2--b3-4--5--b6-b7-1--2--b3-4--5--b6-b7-1--1--b7-b6-5--4--b3-2--1--b7-b6-5--4--b3-2--1--|\nFng|1--3--4--1--3--4--1--3--1--2--4--1--2--4--1--1--4--2--1--4--2--1--3--1--4--3--1--4--3--1--|\ne  |------------------------------------------7--7--------------------------------------------|\nB  |---------------------------------7--8--10-------10-8--7-----------------------------------|\nG  |------------------------6--7--9--------------------------9--7--6--------------------------|\nD  |------------------7--9--------------------------------------------9--7--------------------|\nA  |---------7--9--10-------------------------------------------------------10-9--7-----------|\nE  |7--9--10-------------------------------------------------------------------------10-9--7--|\nReturn to the low root; release pressure; move the entire frame one fret.\nD-start and U-start","text_sha256":"be14552a29334fa60ea191a800a0bdd3dc65260e81ad22eb69049df9317c6854"},"L22-PDF-GUIDANCE":{"format":"pdf","page":1,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/PDF version/Scale_Exercises_Section_III_Level_22_Natural_Minor_Two_Octave_Six_String_Neck_Ladder.pdf","sha256":"f07518814be26b8290c6b9a688251eb77fd2b2aedb8efc03a0469167d8be7bde","text":"Scale Exercises - Section III, Level 22\nNatural Minor Two-Octave Six-String Neck Ladder: A to A\nExtend the exact Level 21 formula across all six strings before moving it one fret.\nThe minor section still starts on A.\n1. Extend the Level 21 shape\nLow E/A: R, R+2, R+3 (1,3,4). D: R, R+2 (1,3). G: R-1,\nR, R+2 (1,2,4). B: R, R+1, R+3 (1,2,4). High e: R (1).\n2. Manage the two upper-string changes\nThe ascent uses 3-3-2-3-3-1 notes per string. Reach\nback one fret on G, then rebuild for the B-string tuning\noffset. Do not hold a static five-fret stretch.\n3. Preserve rhythm and pick cycle\nRepeat the high root at the turn. The complete up/down\ncell contains an even 30 notes, so every new key\nbegins with the same pick orientation.\nWorked example - A natural minor at low-E fret 5\nScale notes: A B C D E F G | A B C D E F G A. The high root is repeated at the turn.\nLOW ROOT -> MIDDLE ROOT -> HIGH ROOT | HIGH ROOT -> MIDDLE ROOT -> LOW ROOT\nDeg|1--2--b3-4--5--b6-b7-1--2--b3-4--5--b6-b7-1--1--b7-b6-5--4--b3-2--1--b7-b6-5--4--b3-2--1--|\nFng|1--3--4--1--3--4--1--3--1--2--4--1--2--4--1--1--4--2--1--4--2--1--3--1--4--3--1--4--3--1--|\ne  |------------------------------------------5--5--------------------------------------------|\nB  |---------------------------------5--6--8--------8--6--5-----------------------------------|\nG  |------------------------4--5--7--------------------------7--5--4--------------------------|\nD  |------------------5--7--------------------------------------------7--5--------------------|\nA  |---------5--7--8--------------------------------------------------------8--7--5-----------|\nE  |5--7--8--------------------------------------------------------------------------8--7--5--|\nKEY ROUTE\nA -> Bb -> B -> C -> C# -> D -> Eb -> E -> F -> F# -> G -> G# -> A, then reverse.\nSPAN AUDIT\nThe map spans R-1 to R+3, but the hand releases and reforms; never clamp a five-fret grip.\nThe fixed shape transposes. A natural minor is the starting rung, not the key of every rung.\nSession protocol\n1\nMaster the A-minor\ntwo-octave cell before\nadding a shift.\n2\nStart 10-15 BPM below\nyour clean Level 21\ntempo.\n3\nUse 2-3 neighboring\nrungs and pause one\nbeat after each cell.\n4\nRepeat with a\ndownstroke start and an\nupstroke start.\n5\nRemove the pause;\nconnect the route and\nreverse at fret 17.\n6\nAdd 2 BPM after 3 clean\ntrips; reduce 4-6 BPM\nafter 2 errors.\nSection III now extends the 6th-string-root natural-minor shape across two full octaves.\nPage 1 of 7","text_sha256":"19516e4962b7e4b290f5197faafabdc0822d16719c234e4ca0c8b809493f9fd0"},"L22-PDF-ROUTE":{"format":"pdf","page":2,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/PDF version/Scale_Exercises_Section_III_Level_22_Natural_Minor_Two_Octave_Six_String_Neck_Ladder.pdf","sha256":"f07518814be26b8290c6b9a688251eb77fd2b2aedb8efc03a0469167d8be7bde","text":"Level 22 - Chromatic Natural-Minor Route\nAscending route: complete each 30-note scale cell, then move the frame +1 fret\nDescending route: use the same cards in reverse order and move -1 fret\nStandard tuning. Two-octave 6th-string-root natural minor. One completed cell = 30 notes.\nPage 2 of 7\nRung\nKey\nLow-E root\nFrame\nScale tones (degrees 1-7)\n01\nA natural minor\nfret 5\n4-8\nA  B  C  D  E  F  G\n02\nBb natural minor\nfret 6\n5-9\nBb  C  Db  Eb  F  Gb  Ab\n03\nB natural minor\nfret 7\n6-10\nB  C#  D  E  F#  G  A\n04\nC natural minor\nfret 8\n7-11\nC  D  Eb  F  G  Ab  Bb\n05\nC# natural minor\nfret 9\n8-12\nC#  D#  E  F#  G#  A  B\n06\nD natural minor\nfret 10\n9-13\nD  E  F  G  A  Bb  C\n07\nEb natural minor\nfret 11\n10-14\nEb  F  Gb  Ab  Bb  Cb  Db\n08\nE natural minor\nfret 12\n11-15\nE  F#  G  A  B  C  D\n09\nF natural minor\nfret 13\n12-16\nF  G  Ab  Bb  C  Db  Eb\n10\nF# natural minor\nfret 14\n13-17\nF#  G#  A  B  C#  D  E\n11\nG natural minor\nfret 15\n14-18\nG  A  Bb  C  D  Eb  F\n12\nG# natural minor\nfret 16\n15-19\nG#  A#  B  C#  D#  E  F#\n13\nA natural minor - octave\nfret 17\n16-20\nA  B  C  D  E  F  G\nHow to use the map\nUp pass:\nrungs 01-13.\nTurn:\nfinish the high-A cell at\nfret 17, then reverse.\nDown pass:\nrungs 12-01. Skip the\nhigh-A card unless\nstarting a new round trip.\nSpan rule:\nR-1 to R+3 is a moving\nframe, not a held\nfive-fret stretch.\nGoal:\nhear the same minor\nformula while both\noctaves rise and fall.\nMastery gate before the next natural-minor level\nName every key before playing it; sing or say 1-2-b3-4-5-b6-b7; keep the G-string backreach relaxed; rebuild the B-string fingering instead of copying G; land each one-fret relocation without\nsliding; preserve equal note length and volume through all six strings; and complete the full fret-5 to fret-17 to fret-5 route with both pick starts.\nROUND-TRIP COUNT\n25 cells x 30 notes = 750 picked notes.","text_sha256":"de608754b20fa11d68f498af191279353383343200b0c4e20542bfa1035c957a"},"L22-TXT-GUIDANCE":{"first_line":1,"format":"txt","last_line":52,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/TXT version/Scale_Exercises_Section_III_Level_22_Natural_Minor_Two_Octave_Six_String_Neck_Ladder.txt","sha256":"0031bdd05834d1f1f381240a48a5fa193da561f7bdf51df580771f593c82b1dc","text":"SCALE EXERCISES - SECTION III, LEVEL 22\nNATURAL MINOR TWO-OCTAVE SIX-STRING NECK LADDER: A TO A\n\nPURPOSE\nExtend the Level 21 natural-minor shape across all six strings and two full octaves. Play the\ncomplete 30-note up/down cell, release pressure, move the entire hand-and-thumb frame exactly one fret,\nand repeat through every natural-minor key. Begin with A natural minor at low-E fret 5, climb to A\nnatural minor at fret 17, then reverse and return one fret at a time.\n\nIMPORTANT INTERPRETATION\nMoving one fixed scale shape by one fret transposes it. A natural minor is the starting rung, not the key\nof every rung. A fixed-key A-minor exercise in every neck position requires changing the note layout and\nremains a separate later branch.\n\nNATURAL-MINOR FORMULA\nDegrees:   1 2 b3 4 5 b6 b7, repeated in the second octave\nIntervals: whole - half - whole - whole - half - whole - whole\n\nTWO-OCTAVE SHAPE - ROOT FRET R ON LOW E\nLow E string: R, R+2, R+3          Fingers 1,3,4\nA string:     R, R+2, R+3          Fingers 1,3,4\nD string:     R, R+2               Fingers 1,3\nG string:     R-1, R, R+2          Fingers 1,2,4\nB string:     R, R+1, R+3          Fingers 1,2,4\nHigh e string:R                     Finger 1\nThe complete map spans R-1 through R+3. Do not hold a static five-fret stretch. Keep the lower-string\nframe relaxed, release pressure for the one-fret G-string backreach, and rebuild the hand for the B string.\n\nSTRING-DISTRIBUTION RULE\nAscending note counts by string: 3 - 3 - 2 - 3 - 3 - 1.\nDescending note counts by string: 1 - 3 - 3 - 2 - 3 - 3.\nThe G string begins one fret below the root reference, and the B-string tuning offset changes the visible\npattern again. Use the assigned fingering rather than copying one string pattern onto the next.\n\nCELL AND PICKING RULE\nAscend from the low root through the middle octave to the high root, repeat the high root at the turn,\nthen descend to the low root. The result is 30 notes, so the next key begins with the same pick orientation.\nD-start: strict D-U alternate picking through every string crossing, the turn, and the one-fret relocation.\nU-start: strict U-D alternate picking through every string crossing, the turn, and the one-fret relocation.\nDo not restart the pick cycle on a new string, at either octave, at the scale turn, or after shifting one fret.\n\nNECK ROUTE\nUP:   A(5) > Bb(6) > B(7) > C(8) > C#(9) > D(10) > Eb(11) > E(12) > F(13) > F#(14) > G(15) > G#(16) > A(17)\nDOWN: A(17) > G#(16) > G(15) > F#(14) > F(13) > E(12) > Eb(11) > D(10) > C#(9) > C(8) > B(7) > Bb(6) > A(5)\n\nPRACTICE RULE\nBegin 10-15 BPM below your clean Level 21 tempo. First master the A-natural-minor cell alone. Then use\n2-3 neighboring rungs, play even eighth notes, and pause one beat after each 30-note cell while moving\nthe complete frame one fret. Repeat with both pick starts. Remove the pause, connect the ladder, reverse\nat fret 17, and return to fret 5. Add 2 BPM after three clean round trips. Reduce 4-6 BPM after two errors,\nstring-crossing noise, dragged backreaches, or rising tension. Advance after the full route is clean with\nboth pick starts on two separate days.","text_sha256":"8a7894e6e7b5e46db83679b895ef0db3dbfb56598e941ae1e7baa852f59325af"},"L22-TXT-RUNG01":{"first_line":55,"format":"txt","last_line":66,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/TXT version/Scale_Exercises_Section_III_Level_22_Natural_Minor_Two_Octave_Six_String_Neck_Ladder.txt","sha256":"0031bdd05834d1f1f381240a48a5fa193da561f7bdf51df580771f593c82b1dc","text":"RUNG 01 OF 13 - A NATURAL MINOR - ROOT ON LOW E FRET 5 - FRAME 4-8\nScale tones across two octaves: A B C D E F G | A B C D E F G A\n30-note cell: low root to high root, repeat the high root, then return to the low root.\nDeg|1--2--b3-4--5--b6-b7-1--2--b3-4--5--b6-b7-1--1--b7-b6-5--4--b3-2--1--b7-b6-5--4--b3-2--1--|\nFng|1--3--4--1--3--4--1--3--1--2--4--1--2--4--1--1--4--2--1--4--2--1--3--1--4--3--1--4--3--1--|\ne  |------------------------------------------5--5--------------------------------------------|\nB  |---------------------------------5--6--8--------8--6--5-----------------------------------|\nG  |------------------------4--5--7--------------------------7--5--4--------------------------|\nD  |------------------5--7--------------------------------------------7--5--------------------|\nA  |---------5--7--8--------------------------------------------------------8--7--5-----------|\nE  |5--7--8--------------------------------------------------------------------------8--7--5--|\nFinish on the low root, release pressure, and move the entire frame one fret in the route direction.","text_sha256":"eea5bd6bd3a47ae86e4fd7777301f85613bcaab6665854711de45146b2b61881"},"L22-TXT-RUNG02":{"first_line":69,"format":"txt","last_line":80,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/TXT version/Scale_Exercises_Section_III_Level_22_Natural_Minor_Two_Octave_Six_String_Neck_Ladder.txt","sha256":"0031bdd05834d1f1f381240a48a5fa193da561f7bdf51df580771f593c82b1dc","text":"RUNG 02 OF 13 - BB NATURAL MINOR - ROOT ON LOW E FRET 6 - FRAME 5-9\nScale tones across two octaves: Bb C Db Eb F Gb Ab | Bb C Db Eb F Gb Ab Bb\n30-note cell: low root to high root, repeat the high root, then return to the low root.\nDeg|1--2--b3-4--5--b6-b7-1--2--b3-4--5--b6-b7-1--1--b7-b6-5--4--b3-2--1--b7-b6-5--4--b3-2--1--|\nFng|1--3--4--1--3--4--1--3--1--2--4--1--2--4--1--1--4--2--1--4--2--1--3--1--4--3--1--4--3--1--|\ne  |------------------------------------------6--6--------------------------------------------|\nB  |---------------------------------6--7--9--------9--7--6-----------------------------------|\nG  |------------------------5--6--8--------------------------8--6--5--------------------------|\nD  |------------------6--8--------------------------------------------8--6--------------------|\nA  |---------6--8--9--------------------------------------------------------9--8--6-----------|\nE  |6--8--9--------------------------------------------------------------------------9--8--6--|\nFinish on the low root, release pressure, and move the entire frame one fret in the route direction.","text_sha256":"a807e7699c06fa75befe07f203e2a3dd3b8780092966a6e581eeb74f3f78fd12"}}},"reference_registry":{"entities":[{"id":"fg:course:000001","kind":"course","label":"Fathom Guitar105","parent":null},{"id":"fg:workbook:000022","kind":"workbook","label":"Legacy Level22","parent":"fg:course:000001"},{"id":"fg:module:001171","kind":"module","label":"Level 22 A to Bb natural-minor two-octave 60-contact neighboring cells","parent":"fg:workbook:000022"},{"id":"fg:item:001171","kind":"item","label":"Level 22 A to Bb natural-minor two-octave 60-contact neighboring cells","parent":"fg:module:001171"},{"id":"fg:variant:007464","kind":"variant","label":"l22-a-bb-neighbor-D-start","parent":"fg:item:001171"},{"id":"fg:variant:007465","kind":"variant","label":"l22-a-bb-neighbor-U-start","parent":"fg:item:001171"}],"identity_version":1,"rules":"Opaque allocated IDs never recomputed from titles, file paths, local code, position in navigation or content hash; parent edges may change only with reviewed provenance. Workbook initial allocations reflect frozen source identities, never renumber."},"resource_plan":{"availability":"required_unsupplied","entry_ids":["R39","R48","R73","R74","R75","R76","R77",